tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2347-lent-kept-where-deleting-it-is-not-the-one-repair.hero:14:20: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `db` of `close` is a word nothing reads — `db` is a handle, the pointer itself, which C receives by value, so nothing is lent — only a `cstr`, a `ptr` or a group's record that is no handle is lent without `@`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2347-lent-kept-where-deleting-it-is-not-the-one-repair.hero:15:19: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `n` of `bump` is a word nothing reads — `n` is not a `cstr`, a `ptr` or a group's record, and only those are lent without `@`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2347-lent-kept-where-deleting-it-is-not-the-one-repair.hero:16:19: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `buf` of `fill` is a word nothing reads — `buf` is a `ptr` that declares no extent, and a `ptr` lend reaches only a parameter declared `counted_by` — nothing is ever lent here, so the word is dead text; write `counted_by <n> lent`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2347-lent-kept-where-deleting-it-is-not-the-one-repair.hero:18:19: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `m` of `size` is a word nothing reads — `m` is not a `cstr`, a `ptr` or a group's record, and only those are lent without `@`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-2347-lent-kept-where-deleting-it-is-not-the-one-repair.hero:18:22: error[ffi_type]: `Mine` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (§4.19)
